Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: land the MoE expert cache provider files
 (VK-MOE-CACHE step 1 of 2 - files, not yet wired)

Three files absent from our tree entirely, taken at TIP state rather than by replaying the cluster history: 539e98959 rewrites what 6723fdfa8 and f3042492d introduced, so a replay would land broken code and then fix it.

The port is add-only and that is VERIFIED, not assumed: ggml/src/ggml-backend-moe-cache.h diverges +56/-0 (the provider-registry API did NOT change) and our ggml/src/ggml-cuda/moe-cache.cu by only 19/-19 cosmetic lines. ggml-moe-cache-common.h states its own rule at its head - the CUDA backend keeps its own copy of these types in moe-cache.cu and must NOT include this header - so our working CUDA file is untouched by this ingest. The provider reaches only public headers (ggml-vulkan.h, ggml-backend-impl.h, ggml-impl.h, ../ggml-quants.h) plus raw Vulkan; it does not reach into ggml-vulkan.cpp internals, which is why our diverged copy of that file does not block it.

